{"verdict": "reject", "tier": "tier2", "summary": "The scripts/auto_phase_continuation.py glob-widening change (PLAN_GLOB -> PLAN_GLOBS, adding *_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_*.yaml) is a small, sound, backward-compatible change, correctly implemented and does not touch .github/workflows/**. However, the core deliverable of this task -- the ChatGPT-vs-Z.AI security audit cross-reference evaluation -- contains a real, verifiable self-consistency defect that undermines trust in the analysis it is meant to authoritatively record. The cross_reference_summary block in SECURITY_AUDIT_EVALUATION_2026-07-25.yaml states raised_by_both_audits: 2, raised_by_chatgpt_only: 3, raised_by_zai_only: 11, which sums to 16 -- not the block's own stated total_distinct_findings_evaluated: 19. Directly tallying each finding's own raised_by field shows 3 findings (SEC-02, SEC-06, SEC-08) are actually tagged raised_by both audits, 4 are ChatGPT-only, and 12 are Z.AI-only (3+4+12=19, correctly totaling). Critically, SEC-08 -- the single highest-severity finding in the whole evaluation (the only one rated 'high': failure-event rate-limiting) -- is explicitly tagged raised_by: [AUDIT-000009, AUDIT-000010] and its own notes field says 'both audits independently flag it,' yet the document's audit_quality_assessment narrative claims only SEC-06 and SEC-02 were raised by both audits, silently omitting SEC-08 and understating cross-audit corroboration on the most important finding. A third, again-different count (2 raised by both, 3 ChatGPT-only, 10 Z.AI-only) appears in MASTER_INDEX.yaml's own scope summary. Since the entire point of this task was to produce an accurate, independently-verified cross-reference between the two audits, and its own headline overlap statistic is internally contradictory in three different places in the diff, this should go back for a correction pass before being handed to a human for sign-off. The remaining findings/phase content otherwise look internally coherent (evidence citations, phase assignments, and the two refuted/two deferred findings' reasoning all check out against the stated file:line evidence), and no .github/workflows changes are present.", "issues": ["cross_reference_summary in ai-os/SECURITY_AUDIT_EVALUATION_2026-07-25.yaml (raised_by_both_audits: 2 / raised_by_chatgpt_only: 3 / raised_by_zai_only: 11) sums to 16, not the block's own total_distinct_findings_evaluated: 19 -- arithmetic does not close.", "Per-finding raised_by tags (ground truth) show 3 findings marked both-audits (SEC-02, SEC-06, SEC-08), not 2 as the summary and audit_quality_assessment narrative claim; SEC-08 -- the single 'high' severity finding -- is one of them, and its own notes field says so explicitly, directly contradicting the narrative text that lists only SEC-06 and SEC-02 as cross-audit-corroborated.", "MASTER_INDEX.yaml's scope field states yet a third, different breakdown ('2 raised by both audits independently, 3 by ChatGPT only, 10 by Z.AI only') that also does not match either the per-finding data or the evaluation file's own cross_reference_summary -- three inconsistent counts of the same metric now exist across the diff.", "Minor: the stale error message at scripts/auto_phase_continuation.py line ~547 still says 'no *_PHASE_PLAN_2026-07-24.yaml files found' even though PLAN_GLOBS now covers two non-date-hardcoded patterns -- cosmetic only, does not affect discover_plan_paths() logic.", "Minor/latent: external_deps_satisfied()'s file_re regex (line ~314) is still hardcoded to match only '..._PHASE_PLAN_2026-07-24.yaml' and was not widened alongside PLAN_GLOBS, so an external_depends_on reference to a 2026-07-25-dated plan or an *_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_*.yaml file would be mechanically unresolvable (treated as UNMET). Not triggered by this plan today (its one depends_on is internal, not external_depends_on) but will silently block a future plan that does reference this one externally."]}
